refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public arrayStreamException::getErrors
Returns all errors reported by the stream operation that threw the exception, both terminating and non-terminating.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 Returns a list of StreamError objects in the
 order in which the errors were reported.

  &reftitle.examples;

   StreamException::getErrors example


<?php
$context = stream_context_create([
    'stream' => [
        'error_mode' => StreamErrorMode::Exception,
    ],
]);

try {
    $stream = fopen('/nonexistent/file.txt', 'r', false, $context);
} catch (StreamException $exception) {
    echo $exception->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;

    foreach ($exception->getErrors() as $error) {
        echo $error->wrapperName, ': ', $error->code->name, PHP_EOL;
    }
}


   &example.outputs;


